# ============================================================
# Recommended .gitignore policy for the AI-config kit
# Policy (2026-09-03): the AI config is NEVER committed. It moves
# between machines only through the export zip + install.sh.
# Append the IGNORE section to your project's .gitignore.
# ============================================================

# ---- IGNORE: the whole AI config (distributed via the export zip) ----
.claude/
.ai/
.cursor/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.mcp.json
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.github/instructions/
.github/prompts/
.github/agents/
.vscode/mcp.json

# ---- IGNORE: machine-local / runtime / secrets (covered above, listed for clarity) ----
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/state/
.claude/agent-memory/
.claude/plans/
.claude/tmp/
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/logs/
.cursor/memory/
.ai/export/*.zip
.ai/export/*.tar.gz
.ai-backup-*/

# ---- IGNORE: keys. Only .env.example (empty values) is tracked ----
.env

# Verify nothing leaked (must print nothing):
#   git ls-files .claude .ai .cursor .github/copilot-instructions.md AGENTS.md CLAUDE.md
#
# Consequence: github.com Copilot (PR review, coding agent) reads only committed
# files, so it will NOT see these rules. Copilot inside VS Code still reads the
# local .github/copilot-instructions.md and AGENTS.md; Claude Code and Cursor are
# unaffected.
